  "confirmed_conclusion": "Generation-time minimization uses per-class probe sets over all instrumented subject classes reached during receiver/argument materialization, focal invocation and result observation. Method scope restricts generation targets, while retained-test usefulness is not restricted to probes of the focal method. Receiver setup can therefore retain tests whose direct focal call repeats the same null-input early return.",
  "s0002_explanation": "The12 retained tests vary receiver constructors/mutator setup while every direct CharBuffer focal call passes null. Whole-class coverage and native probes can increase without improving the focal2/15 lines and1/12 branches. This is consistent with and supported by the confirmed broader minimization objective; case count must not be treated as focal testing quality.",
  "limits": [
    "Per-test sandbox probe BitSets are not persisted in these artifacts, so the exact incremental probe contribution and retaining reason of each of the12 tests cannot be reconstructed without new execution.",
    "This evidence does not establish why non-null CharBuffer candidates were never generated, failed construction, or were not retained; internal candidate-cause remains unknown.",
    "The greedy minimizer has a special one-per-method/outcome rule for completely empty probe maps; this does not narrow its main class-wide probe criterion.",
    "Symbolic uncovered-line steering separately slices focal method lines, so broad minimization does not imply every steering stage ignores the focal method."
